## Catch2 Basics for AlpacaCore

### Basic Test Structure

```cpp
// tests/test_zwo_camera.cpp
#include <catch2/catch_all.hpp>
#include <alpacacore/camera_driver.h>
#include <alpacacore/vendor/zwo/zwo_camera_driver.h>

TEST_CASE("ZWO Camera Driver - Basic Operations", "[zwo][camera]") {
    // Test code here
}
```

### Test Tags

Tags are used to organize and filter tests:

- **Vendor tags**: `[zwo]`, `[qhy]`, `[ioptron]` - Identify vendor-specific tests
- **Device tags**: `[camera]`, `[telescope]`, `[focuser]` - Identify device type
- **Test type tags**: `[unit]`, `[integration]`, `[hardware]` - Identify test category
- **Status tags**: `[!mayfail]`, `[!shouldfail]` - Mark expected failures

**Example**:
```cpp
TEST_CASE("ZWO Camera - Exposure Test", "[zwo][camera][unit]") {
    // Unit test
}

TEST_CASE("ZWO Camera - Hardware Integration", "[zwo][camera][integration][hardware]") {
    // Integration test requiring hardware
}
```

### Assertions

**REQUIRE** (stops on failure):
```cpp
REQUIRE(driver.get_connected() == true);
REQUIRE_THROWS_AS(driver.start_exposure(-1.0, true), AlpacaException);
REQUIRE_THROWS_WITH(driver.start_exposure(-1.0, true), "Invalid exposure duration");
```

**CHECK** (continues on failure):
```cpp
CHECK(driver.get_name() == "ZWO ASI294MC Pro");
CHECK(driver.get_device_type() == DeviceType::Camera);
```

**Floating Point Comparisons**:
```cpp
#include <cmath>

REQUIRE(std::abs(driver.get_temperature() - 25.5) < 0.1);  // Within 0.1°C
REQUIRE(driver.get_exposure_time() == Approx(1.0).margin(0.001));  // Within 0.001s
```

### Sections

Use `SECTION` to test multiple scenarios within one test case:

```cpp
TEST_CASE("ZWO Camera - Connection States", "[zwo][camera]") {
    auto driver = create_zwo_camera(0, 0);
    
    SECTION("Initially disconnected") {
        REQUIRE(driver->get_connected() == false);
    }
    
    SECTION("Connect successfully") {
        driver->set_connected(true);
        REQUIRE(driver->get_connected() == true);
    }
    
    SECTION("Disconnect after connect") {
        driver->set_connected(true);
        driver->set_connected(false);
        REQUIRE(driver->get_connected() == false);
    }
}
```

