## Quick Reference

### Test File Template

```cpp
#include <catch2/catch_all.hpp>
#include <alpacacore/<device>_driver.h>
#include <alpacacore/vendor/<vendor>/<vendor>_<device>_driver.h>
#include <alpacacore/util/error_handling.h>

TEST_CASE("<Vendor> <Device> - <Feature>", "[vendor][device][unit]") {
    // Test code
}
```

### Common Assertions

```cpp
REQUIRE(condition);                    // Assert and stop on failure
CHECK(condition);                     // Assert and continue on failure
REQUIRE_THROWS_AS(expr, Exception);   // Assert exception type
REQUIRE_THROWS_WITH(expr, "message"); // Assert exception message
REQUIRE_NOTHROW(expr);                // Assert no exception
SKIP("reason");                        // Skip test with reason
```

### Test Tags

- `[vendor]` - Vendor name (zwo, qhy, ioptron)
- `[device]` - Device type (camera, telescope, focuser)
- `[unit]` - Unit test (no hardware)
- `[integration]` - Integration test
- `[hardware]` - Requires physical hardware
- `[mock]` - Uses mocked dependencies
- `[performance]` - Performance/benchmark test

### Running Tests

```bash
# All tests
ctest

# Specific tags
./tests/alpacacore_tests [zwo][camera]

# Exclude tags
./tests/alpacacore_tests ~[hardware]

# List all tests
./tests/alpacacore_tests --list-tests

# Verbose output
./tests/alpacacore_tests --success
```

